{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the silver of them that were numbered of the congregation.</b> It does not say 'silver of the terumah' nor 'silver of the wave offering,' as it says 'bronze of the wave offering' — to tell you that the silver of the congregation's census goes toward this census exactly as needed for the work of the Tabernacle in precise measure. And with the silver and bronze Scripture explains what was done with them, because most of the vessels were made from them; but with the gold it did not explain, because no complete vessel was made from it — only the Menorah and the cover and the plating for the planks, for the bars, for the golden altar, and for the table. Come and see how beloved is the Tabernacle, for it parallels the creation of the world. How so? On the first day: בראשית את השמים, and it is written: נוטה שמים כיריעה — and corresponding to this, for the Tabernacle: ועשית יריעות עזים. On the second: יהי רקיע ויהי מבדיל — and corresponding to it: והבדילה הפרכת לכם. On the third: יקוו המים — and corresponding to it: ועשית כיור, where the waters are gathered. On the fourth: יהי מאורות — and corresponding to them: ועשית מנורת זהב. On the fifth: ישרצו המים ועוף יעופף — and corresponding to it: והיו הכרובים פורשי כנפים. On the sixth: Adam was created — and corresponding to it: ואתה הקרב אליך את אהרן אחיך. On the seventh: ויכלו — and corresponding to it: ותכל. There it is written: ויברך אלהים — and corresponding to it: ויברך אותם משה. There it is written: ויקדש אותו — and corresponding to it: וימשח אותו ויקדש אותו. Corresponding to the heavens: the Holy of Holies, where the Shechinah of the Holy One, blessed be He, resides. Corresponding to the earth and the fruit of the earth: the table and the two arrangements of the showbread — the six arrangements corresponding to the six seasons: sowing and harvest, cold and heat, summer and winter."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:54.610040095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}